        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are proud to present 23 Rushbrook Avenue to the market. This is a highly impressive 3-bedroom semi-detached west facing home that combines excellent presentation with a particularly versatile layout. This beautifully appointed property is presented in pristine turnkey condition, having undergone a comprehensive renovation in 2019 and benefiting from a B2 BER rating. Perfectly suited to buyers seeking a home of quality that can be enjoyed immediately, the converted attic further enhances the property, providing a highly versatile additional space.\r\n\r\nAt ground floor level, the home is centred around a bright and beautifully considered open-plan kitchen and dining area, complemented by a separate living room and guest WC, all with underfloor heating. The first floor provides three well-proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom, while the converted attic offers an excellent additional room, ideal as a family room, home office or playroom. Throughout, the accommodation has been thoughtfully designed to maximise both style and functionality, with beautiful oak flooring running through the ground floor, elegant pocket doors connecting the living and dining spaces and a feature gas fireplace. Every element has been carefully considered and cleverly integrated, creating a home that is as practical as it is visually appealing.\r\n\r\nThe property has been thoughtfully designed to provide ample storage throughout, with bespoke cabinetry incorporating integrated storage within the kitchen bench, hallway wardrobes, and additional luggage storage cleverly built into the eaves along the staircase leading to the attic.\r\n\r\nThe dining area opens through bi-fold doors onto the adjoining external decking, creating a seamless connection with the west-facing garden beyond. A particular highlight of the property, the garden enjoys an abundance of afternoon and evening sunshine and is framed by mature hedging, with a substantial block-built shed providing excellent additional storage.\r\n\r\nThe garden shed has also been renovated, featuring a new roof and double glazed window, as well as full plumbing and electrical connections. It provides a versatile additional space that can be utilised as a utility room, while also offering valuable extra storage.\r\n\r\nThe property is ideally positioned in this well-established part of Templeogue, offering a mature residential setting with an excellent range of amenities close at hand. Orwell Shopping Centre is within easy reach, while both Templeogue and Terenure Villages provide a wide selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and local services. Tymon Park is just moments from the front door, offering extensive walks, playing pitches, playgrounds and recreational facilities, with Bushy Park and Dodder Valley Park also nearby. The area is particularly well served for families, with a host of excellent schools within easy reach, including St. Mac Dara’s Community College, approximately 200 metres from the property.\r\n\r\nThe location is highly convenient for commuters, with easy access to the M50 and a strong selection of public transport options. Dublin Bus routes include the F2, 82, 15a, 150, F1, A1 and A3, providing connections towards the city centre, Rathmines, Terenure, Tallaght, and further. \r\n\r\nTempleogue offers an appealing balance between established residential living and accessibility to the city. The surrounding area has a strong selection of sports clubs, parks, schools, shopping and leisure facilities, while Templeogue Village, Orwell Shopping Centre and nearby Terenure provide plenty of everyday conveniences.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\nGround Floor\t\r\nLiving Room - 3.38m x 4.31m\r\nKitchen - 3.40m x 3.31m\r\nDining Area - 3.00m x 3.31m\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.98m x 3.35m\r\nBedroom 2 - 3.61m x 3.58m\r\nBedroom 3 - 2.80m x 2.47m\r\nBathroom - 2.31m x 2.14m\r\n\r\nSecond Floor\r\nConverted Attic - 5.74m x 3.63m\r\n\r\nLocal area\r\nSchools: Bishop Galvin, Bishop Shanahan, Riverview Educate Together, St. Mac Dara's, St Pauls, Templeogue College, Our Ladys’, Terenure College, and many more nearby\r\nBus routes (within 10 mins): F2, 82, 15a, 150, F1, A1 and A3\r\n\r\nProperty features\r\nc. 113 sq. m. (1,216 sq. ft.)\r\nGFCH with underfloor heating with multi zone controls.\r\nB2 – BER rating\r\nOff street parking\r\nYear of construction: c. 1983\r\n\r\nKey Features\r\nLarge converted attic\r\nWest-facing rear garden \r\nTop turnkey condition \r\nBright open-plan kitchen/dining area \r\nSeparate living room \r\nBrick-built garden shed and mature rear hedging \r\nOff-street parking\r\nGround floor guest WC \r\nConvenient access to the M50 \r\nExcellent choice of local schools and amenities"
      },
